[{:db/id "q-73399/selection/54ac610d4774fee0ede6478b691a6eacc7c927529e978f51a18e757cb18525eb" :answer/id #uuid "d9e0e7e0-d0d2-5d00-be37-746b1796e279" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=3$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73399/selection/5d44250d7e508234b297484ad78b3f7e8610b52e4b4d5ab98b8660008c954e0b" :answer/id #uuid "484d8f9b-d06a-5592-a30b-47258a4acfdc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=3$ and $x=7$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73399/selection/3ac5142ba5d5a5b63c0beda9e8b47ba7ecdb42c6fbabf2b2963e45310d94e568" :answer/id #uuid "e01eed10-4f2d-50b4-ae2f-8468ea94f0de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=7$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73399/selection/8dd0139fe2bdff82a7de02af21e81b3fb0031e695d60709e4cec3b9cfa395bee" :answer/id #uuid "3bd1b7ee-b130-5178-809d-86ca37411752" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-1$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73399/selection/523c05f2cbc43372eff755b4c7fa1de31ccec29f1e34b4948b141f0df8b89ffb" :answer/id #uuid "a8b16167-95ec-5d45-a09a-860730a4ddff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-1$  and $x=7$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73399/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "db7b9a07-56fe-5751-bb1b-51c088e24cdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73399/selection/5d44250d7e508234b297484ad78b3f7e8610b52e4b4d5ab98b8660008c954e0b" :answer-field/choices ["q-73399/selection/54ac610d4774fee0ede6478b691a6eacc7c927529e978f51a18e757cb18525eb" "q-73399/selection/5d44250d7e508234b297484ad78b3f7e8610b52e4b4d5ab98b8660008c954e0b" "q-73399/selection/3ac5142ba5d5a5b63c0beda9e8b47ba7ecdb42c6fbabf2b2963e45310d94e568" "q-73399/selection/8dd0139fe2bdff82a7de02af21e81b3fb0031e695d60709e4cec3b9cfa395bee" "q-73399/selection/523c05f2cbc43372eff755b4c7fa1de31ccec29f1e34b4948b141f0df8b89ffb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73399" :question/id #uuid "ece606bc-4b2a-5813-a3c1-ba2ac8790c10" :question/math-academy-id "q-73399" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980112/assets/432991e403167bd560517072d24058c3f2106f093cdcad08f3b5f0ed486f9504.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. What are the $x$-coordinates of the critical points?" :question/worked-solution "The critical points of $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ where ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(x)$ doesn't exist. Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal or where the tangent does not exist, respectively. \n\nIn the given graph, we can see that \n\n- at $x=3$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${f}^{′}(3)=0,$ while\n\n- at $x=7$ there is a discontinuity, so  ${f}^{′}(7)$ doesn't exist.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980112/assets/e035d64e759108be78c54d0d8d1018906ef253bdcdaff548edd185b8b6543505.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, there are two critical points, and their $x$-coordinates are $x=3$ and $x=7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73399/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b5ea4a7-acc4-5825-b6c5-b6c87e6a1674"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73399"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73410/selection/f4699282d91b09943f25edea1c300cc58a14ef9a5b0f710fa5d016c2581360b7" :answer/id #uuid "afb79966-ed68-5f2c-a1bb-8d8a256df246" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=3$ and $x=4$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73410/selection/54ac610d4774fee0ede6478b691a6eacc7c927529e978f51a18e757cb18525eb" :answer/id #uuid "6b7d219a-7641-5c12-bde8-d0293a6991df" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=3$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73410/selection/96ff03e219e3cc4c9054e5b5a1d598103847625fe5111224c72202e740b4c3c3" :answer/id #uuid "b5cc5877-0fd0-55f0-b3d5-948650662c0b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All points in the open interval $(3,4)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73410/selection/c00b423d38fc022695304b5623f8f16d80f952174b860c25dbbf7c6f3e0429ea" :answer/id #uuid "3db9a6ff-5921-53c5-8477-0d996f15af4a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=4$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73410/selection/783d60f7d11c6411e5bebf7b612cdc7b895c7efe2ba77201f88851e760fa543e" :answer/id #uuid "19ef078c-fc7b-5dc6-b320-c7b3822c1831" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=3$, $x=4$, and $x=6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73410/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "57b8d7f0-90ca-560f-832e-286b4995ff94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73410/selection/96ff03e219e3cc4c9054e5b5a1d598103847625fe5111224c72202e740b4c3c3" :answer-field/choices ["q-73410/selection/f4699282d91b09943f25edea1c300cc58a14ef9a5b0f710fa5d016c2581360b7" "q-73410/selection/54ac610d4774fee0ede6478b691a6eacc7c927529e978f51a18e757cb18525eb" "q-73410/selection/96ff03e219e3cc4c9054e5b5a1d598103847625fe5111224c72202e740b4c3c3" "q-73410/selection/c00b423d38fc022695304b5623f8f16d80f952174b860c25dbbf7c6f3e0429ea" "q-73410/selection/783d60f7d11c6411e5bebf7b612cdc7b895c7efe2ba77201f88851e760fa543e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73410" :question/id #uuid "a831b1fe-cda9-5ab9-bf01-7acc19edee37" :question/math-academy-id "q-73410" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980112/assets/eab84ed04b86678fb4a8d23c010e9a22beead062595b49818ac95e996c3173e6.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is shown above. What are the $x$-coordinates of all the stationary points?" :question/worked-solution "The stationary points of $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal.\n\nIn the given graph, we can see that at any point between $x=3$ and $x=4$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at those points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980112/assets/ab200bebf80bbd1abe6e0c43ec124fe359da25f38d4346d25d8741decc88aa26.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinates of the stationary points of $f(x)$, are all values in the open interval $(3,4).$ \n\n**Note:** At $x=3$ and $x=4$, there are sharp corners, so ${f}^{′}(x)$ doesn't exist at those points. This gives us two more critical points. But they are not stationary points." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73410/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b5ea4a7-acc4-5825-b6c5-b6c87e6a1674"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73410"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103432/selection/263f2834c39a884ed4107d93e45891bf1c03e1239f1b605574fb2a4e7fa704de" :answer/id #uuid "19509a20-4416-55b8-985a-d2da1754bcc4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-2$ and $x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103432/selection/5eb1c3c8e1fc470bac98d5c8a7260279bce385d35b1b71ec6573d405882929fe" :answer/id #uuid "5093fe11-129e-5e5a-918a-c8885801b1ba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All points in the open interval $(-2,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103432/selection/2a919a38dcf40bf077b56950afd1227bae42613f89d1f943f8c66d5026909718" :answer/id #uuid "56caf002-ef8f-5f09-a5b4-d1138de10f47" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All points in the closed interval $[-2,2]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103432/selection/c79ffc6664a269adaafc63898a2b275e93be9399a3dcc957c87628ef929bc5d0" :answer/id #uuid "cb112ede-bd16-5541-9627-5700d8f98df2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All points in the intervals $(-5,-2)$ and $(2,5)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103432/selection/719a058e5bbf7d63af6718dd2cb7d51c44ca264a9ba6fe2cf04d203dd3650825" :answer/id #uuid "8c3de4b7-7d09-56a4-80a5-4dd4b5b6e3b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All points in the closed intervals $(-5,-2]$ and $[2,5)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103432/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5aa1f45-10ca-521e-9aff-a2310eeeead9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103432/selection/c79ffc6664a269adaafc63898a2b275e93be9399a3dcc957c87628ef929bc5d0" :answer-field/choices ["q-103432/selection/263f2834c39a884ed4107d93e45891bf1c03e1239f1b605574fb2a4e7fa704de" "q-103432/selection/5eb1c3c8e1fc470bac98d5c8a7260279bce385d35b1b71ec6573d405882929fe" "q-103432/selection/2a919a38dcf40bf077b56950afd1227bae42613f89d1f943f8c66d5026909718" "q-103432/selection/c79ffc6664a269adaafc63898a2b275e93be9399a3dcc957c87628ef929bc5d0" "q-103432/selection/719a058e5bbf7d63af6718dd2cb7d51c44ca264a9ba6fe2cf04d203dd3650825"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103432" :question/id #uuid "399a7648-b41d-51df-9f7e-45ef9ac8e709" :question/math-academy-id "q-103432" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980112/assets/55d089ab7c7947e3f9d67a11fd69fa3903abd6f10ef09853fe018eaa16524ec1.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is shown above. What are the $x$-coordinates of all the stationary points?" :question/worked-solution "The stationary points of $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal.\n\nIn the given graph, we can see that\n\n- at any point between $x=-5$ and $x=-2$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at those points,\n\n- at any point between $x=2$ and $x=5$ the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at those points,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980112/assets/6983f3615bf721529173c11de3a9218962a57e4be5247f4bda1ac2fa496531ee.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinates of the stationary points of $f(x)$ are all values in the intervals $(-5,-2)$ and $(2,5).$ \n\n**Note:** At $x=-2$ and $x=2$, there are sharp corners, so ${f}^{′}(x)$ doesn't exist at those points. This gives us two more critical points, but they are not stationary points." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103432/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b5ea4a7-acc4-5825-b6c5-b6c87e6a1674"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103432"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73409/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" :answer/id #uuid "cd25040a-e948-5636-bdbe-1cc158adf2f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73409/selection/bbb90a374934c6ff8be3fc8957c3dd7cb1fbd89fa59adb71945ee9c25ce429ad" :answer/id #uuid "b1ed7f70-685a-5c90-960a-8487eb65e6b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All points in the closed interval $[2,6]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73409/selection/0b71ed31b54db2f2e7ec707b0a04499a5069d7189b0811622a9ab373f5143838" :answer/id #uuid "4c677eed-072e-5a9d-ba1e-38ed2a01a256" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=6$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73409/selection/b3f3cd259eab6f19c0c66e87049fb8d420b48392fd29c0b9bdd7146165731a8c" :answer/id #uuid "e4fb4479-a57e-50a2-8f0e-db3cffbe2cc2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=6$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73409/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "6b655f12-b071-5d9e-89b0-51c0d15f6c03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73409/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "09e609df-9895-5b71-b35b-1a65a8539dcf" :answer-field/key "selection" 